  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which of the following reagent is used for the following reaction?</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>?</mo></mover><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "o9uKb",
      "text": "Copper at high temperature and pressure",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zFISm",
      "text": "Manganese acetate",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dJJTo",
      "text": "Molybdenum oxide",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Bvyvr",
      "text": "Potassium permanganate",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Mo</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mover><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>The reagent used will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Mo</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;(molybdenum oxide) as this reagent always used to oxidise alkanes to aldehyde. So, it is widely used as&nbsp;an oxidation catalyst for acid-mediated catalytic reactions.</p>",
